---
title: dinyd · references in documents
config:
  look: handDrawn
  handDrawnSeed: 5
  theme: dark
  themeVariables:
    mainBkg: "#333333"
    clusterBkg: "#242424"
  themeCSS: |
    small { display: inline-block; text-align: left; }
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 300
---
%% Behavior authority: this diagram.
%% References live only inline in documents. Nothing goes in code files or in a separate mapping file. The code → claim direction is obtained by scanning documents.
%% Notation: in md an anchor is an HTML comment (#lt;!-- … --#gt;), skipped inside code blocks (fenced · indented) and inline code. In .mermaid it is an own-line %% comment, and leading frontmatter is skipped. The documents checked are tracked *.md · *.mermaid.
%% selector = path#location. The path is the Git path from the repository root, with / as the only separator. A path containing ./ · .. · \ · whitespace · --> · %% is malformed. The location may contain spaces (CSS descendant selectors, etc.). Line numbers are not used.
%% Code symbol members that share a name (overloads) are ambiguous and therefore unresolved. An explicit Verify(*) groups the same-named members, in source order, into one region.
%% apply chooses the mode. The default is per format (s1 when structural normalization exists, otherwise b1), and apply --bytes chooses b1. s1 carries tokens and nesting but not node kind names. Whitespace and line breaks between tokens are ignored; the contents of strings · scalars · comments are kept verbatim, inner whitespace included, and comments count as tokens. An s1 recorded for a target without structural normalization is unresolved. b1 is the bytes with only CRLF→LF changed. The digest is the first 16 hex digits of SHA-256, and check recomputes it with the recorded mode.
%% A hand-written digest anchor without a digest is undeclared, and update fills it.
flowchart LR
  Example["Example<br/><small>#lt;!-- dinyd: Hasher.cs#PasswordHasher.Verify s1:3f9a0c1d2e4b5a6c --#gt;</small>"]

  subgraph DigestAnchor["digest anchor · a claim restating code facts"]
    D1["dinyd:"] --> D2["selector"] --> D3["mode:digest<br/><small>s1 structural · b1 bytes</small>"]
  end

  subgraph RefAnchor["delegation · a claim like 'X owns the behavior'"]
    R1["dinyd-ref:"] --> R2["selector<br/><small>may name a directory · no digest</small>"]
  end

  Where["selector = path#location<br/><small>• code symbol · C# · TS · Vue · JS · Go<br/>• JSON · YAML pointer<br/>• CSS rule<br/>• no location: the whole file</small>"]

  Example -.- DigestAnchor
  D2 -.- Where
  R2 -.- Where

  classDef em fill:#173d25,stroke:#86efac
  class DigestAnchor em
